---
source: crates/observed_macros_impl/tests/expansion.rs
expression: output
---
---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(v)] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: i64 }

---- yields ----
`#[counter(...)]` requires field `v` to be a unsigned integer type (u8, u16, u32, u64, usize)

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[updown_counter(v)] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
`#[updown_counter(...)]` requires field `v` to be a signed integer type (i8, i16, i32, i64, isize)

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(v)] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: String }

---- yields ----
`#[counter(v)]` requires field `v` to be a numeric type that `observed::Value` can carry (i8, i16, i32, i64, isize, u8, u16, u32, u64, usize, f32, f64)

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(v)] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: (u8, u8) }

---- yields ----
`#[counter(v)]` requires field `v` to be a numeric type that `observed::Value` can carry (i8, i16, i32, i64, isize, u8, u16, u32, u64, usize, f32, f64)

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(v)] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u128 }

---- yields ----
`#[counter(v)]` does not support 128-bit integers; no telemetry backend represents them, so `observed::Value` has no conversion. Use a 64-bit width instead

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[updown_counter(v)] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: i128 }

---- yields ----
`#[updown_counter(v)]` does not support 128-bit integers; no telemetry backend represents them, so `observed::Value` has no conversion. Use a 64-bit width instead

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(v)] struct Subject { v: u64 }

---- yields ----
`#[counter(v)]` requires field `v` to be `#[unredacted]`; a classified value is rendered through the redaction engine as a string, which carries no measurement for the instrument to record

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(v)] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: Option<u64> }

---- yields ----
`#[counter(v)]` requires field `v` to hold a value on every emission, but it is an `Option<T>`; a metric value cannot be optional. Use a non-optional field, or record it as a metric dimension instead (`#[dimension(metric = ...)]`)

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(v)] struct Subject { #[dimension(metric)] #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
field `v` cannot be both a metric value and a metric dimension (`#[dimension(metric = ...)]`)
